# why: Less talking to Google in the background (apps-repo review, measured with a net log in the twin): no FCM
# invalidation listeners (cloud policy and remote commands, which a TV never has; they checked in and registered
# with android.clients.google.com and mtalk.google.com at every start), no requests to accounts.google.com while no
# OAuth client is set up (ListAccounts at every start; signing in can't work without keys, and with the user's own
# keys the block steps aside), and no on-device AI models manifest (update.googleapis.com and edgedl.me.gvt1.com at
# every start). Web push for sites still works through GCM.
diff --git a/src/chrome/browser/component_updater/optimization_guide_on_device_model_installer.cc b/src/chrome/browser/component_updater/optimization_guide_on_device_model_installer.cc
